WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.670
One day, as the recording
of the new single approached,

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.130
Mitsuki was called out by
Dr. Wakaoji.

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:07.500
But this was a trap set by
a tabloid magazine.

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:10.670
It was devised to photograph
a scandal involving Full Moon.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.630
Gosh! It was an important time
before the recording!

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:15.030
But with words of encouragement
from Dr. Wakaoji,

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:16.600
Mitsuki's fears disappeared and

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:19.630
she resonated with an incredible
singing voice at the recording!

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.800
So, I wonder what's going to
happen today...

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:28.670
Got that?

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:29.700
Yes.

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:17.760
Excuse me...

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:19.560
Huh?! One right now?

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:27.430
Excuse me, are you going to
tell me to pose or anything?

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:29.360
You can do whatever you want,

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.300
if you want to move,
you can move.

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.500
If you're tired, you can rest!

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:47.130
Hey, is this okay?

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:50.360
It's going to be used
for the CD jacket.

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:53.030
The camera's a disposable one too.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.600
That's probably her vision.

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:56.260
Huh?

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:59.530
Don't you think Mitsuki's natural
charm comes out more this way?

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:01.060
Do you think so?

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:02.300
I don't know.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.330
Nice scent.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:08.230
Hey, do you know?

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:10.830
The language of flowers for cosmos.

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:11.730
No.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:16.100
"Young girl's sincerity."
It's perfect for you.

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:33.130
Hey, Takuto.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:34.100
What?

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:36.400
Do you want to go to the
amusement park or something?

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:37.160
Why?

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:41.400
Mitsuki's photo shoot for
the second CD's jacket is over,

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:43.900
so that means we did good work.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:46.730
Then why don't you invite her?

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:50.900
Gosh, you don't understand
a girl's heart at all.

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:52.960
A girl's heart?

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:59.730
Indeed, things that change are
a girl's heart and the autumn sky.

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:03.100
What? Is that a haiku?

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:05.830
– We're here.
– Hello!

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:08.760
Hey, I was waiting for all of you.

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:10.000
Come on up, come on up.

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:16.000
Say, guess who I saw?!

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:17.200
What are they doing?

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:19.160
It's probably a study session.

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:21.030
Hey, look, look.

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:23.230
This is so cute.

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:24.300
You're right.

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:28.860
Nice sound.

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:30.260
Yeah, really.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:33.000
Both of you! Work over here too.

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:34.460
– Okay.
– Okay.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:37.660
Hey Kumi, if I remember,
you do this one like this?

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:38.730
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:41.500
Huh? Kumi, don't you do it like this?

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:43.130
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:45.400
– Well, which one is it?!
– Well, which one is it?!

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:46.630
– Kumi!
– Kumi!

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:48.830
Oh?! What, what?

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:50.300
– Jeez!
– Jeez!

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.860
Kumi, you seem to have no energy.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:56.030
Do you think so?

00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:58.530
Oww!

00:04:58.560 --> 00:04:59.730
Sorry, sorry!

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:01.360
It's the usual, Kumi.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:02.830
Seems like it.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.200
Oh, I can't draw well.

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:11.760
In that case, it's good to
use some picture as a reference.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.900
– How can I do this?
– Oops, a mistake!

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:28.660
Hey! Look at this!

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:30.030
Huh? What?

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:31.000
What? What?

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:33.930
Ta-da! Who is this?

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:36.830
Oh, who is this boy?
So cute.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:39.730
Hey, the girl next to him is Mitsuki.

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:41.000
You're right!

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:43.200
– Then, this is...
– Then, this is...

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:47.900
– Who is this boy?
– Who is this boy?

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:50.500
Oh! Well, that is...that is...

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:54.430
– Mitsuki!
– Mitsuki!

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:57.030
Why did it happen like this?

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:02.830
Therefore, Eichi departed for America.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.330
Wonderful!

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:05.830
So that's what happened.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:08.230
It's a story you can cry about,

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:10.130
no matter how many times
you listen to it.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:12.430
What's wrong, Takuto?

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:16.000
Is this something that you'd
normally talk about so frankly?!

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:16.730
Huh?

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:20.160
I mean it's not a thing to
chatter about with other people.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:23.360
Those kinds of precious memories
should be stored

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.260
quietly inside your heart!

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:26.460
Don't you think so?

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:29.000
M-Maybe...

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:32.230
Man! I don't understand
a girl's heart!

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:33.400
That's incredible!

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:35.060
How romantic!

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:39.760
It's such a surprise that a girl
like that is in our class.

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:43.360
Oh, my dream,
reach beyond the Pacific Ocean.

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:46.030
Reach beyond!

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:49.560
Wait!

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:53.530
Surely, the ending will be Eichi
mounted on a white horse,

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:55.960
arriving to pick up Mitsuki!

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:58.930
Now Mitsuki, take my hand.

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:00.760
Yes...Eichi...

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:11.060
I wish I could love like that!

00:07:13.730 --> 00:07:14.800
Now, now!

00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:18.400
Starting today, for one week,
we will start a mini-corner with Full Moon,

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:22.900
who has set the release for
her second CD, "Eternal Snow."

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:24.660
Now, please take it away, Full Moon.

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:28.330
Yes, it's "Full Moon's
Eternal Correspondence!"

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:30.760
That's a title, left as it is.

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:31.760
Yeah...

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:38.160
Now, to the next fax-mail.
It's from radio name, "Girl Sanshiro."

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:40.560
"Hello, Miss Full Moon."

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:43.430
"I have been a big fan of
you since your debut."

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:44.830
Thank you very much.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:48.160
"To tell you the truth,
I have somebody I like right now."

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:49.130
Wow.

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:52.660
"I was not aware of it until now."

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:57.200
"But recently, I saw his cool appearance
and fell in love with him."

00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:02.300
"And I want to confess to him,
but please tell me what I should do."

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.100
Well, you know,
in this kind of circumstance...

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:12.730
If you believe...
your feelings will reach...him...

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:13.760
I think...

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:16.560
I'm sorry, I wasn't able
to answer very well,

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:18.030
but please try your best.

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:22.200
Now, I will give my song
as a present to Miss Girl Sanshiro.

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:24.930
This is Full Moon's "Eternal Snow."

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:31.700
Good morning, Kumi.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:34.760
Oh... G-Good morning!

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:37.500
What's wrong, Kumi?

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:39.300
You've been acting weird
since last time.

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:49.560
Hey! Hey wait, Kumi!
We have school, school!

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:52.330
Please Mitsuki,
come with me a little bit!

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:00.830
Hey Mitsuki, what do you think

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:04.030
"if you believe, your feeling
will reach him" means?

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:04.730
What?

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:11.100
W-Well, Full Moon was saying something
like that on the radio yesterday.

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:17.460
Do you think it means waiting
until the other person realizes?

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:20.460
Or is there an even deeper meaning?

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:24.230
I don't think it has
such a deep meaning!

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:25.060
Huh?

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:28.630
Well, you know, I was also
listening to the radio show.

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:30.460
And that answer by Full Moon

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:33.760
felt like she didn't know
that much about romance.

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:35.860
Do you think so?

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:38.360
Yeah. If she were knowledgeable,

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:41.660
she would have given
better advice, yup!

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:43.100
Really?

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:46.430
Mitsuki, you understand because
you're an expert on romance.

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:47.160
What?!

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:50.500
Hey Mitsuki!
I want you to be my advisor,

00:09:50.530 --> 00:09:52.260
as the master of romance!

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:55.230
H-Hey Kumi, you're misunderstanding
something.

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:58.300
I'm not an expert on romance.

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:04.760
Actually, I was the one
who faxed Full Moon yesterday.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:07.860
What?! Then you're Girl Sanshiro?

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:12.400
Yeah. I've been doing judo
since I was little.

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:23.760
Please! Please give me advice,
I don't have anybody else!

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:27.430
Well, you know... If there's
something that I can do...

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:29.060
Oh my...

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:30.460
I don't know what's gonna happen.

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:32.560
And, who is the other person?

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:36.160
Machida...

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:40.700
So it was Machida.

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:43.360
Until recently...

00:10:47.860 --> 00:10:48.700
<i>There!</i>

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:58.760
<i>Ouch!</i>

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:04.260
<i>You dummy!</i>

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:05.830
<i>Shut up, you!</i>

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:08.330
It was like that, but...

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:17.430
<i>Kumi, are you really going</i>
<i>to jump over that?</i>

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:20.900
<i>Don't worry, don't worry.</i>
<i>Just watch and see.</i>

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:29.660
<i>She flew over.</i>

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:31.660
<i>That's incredible, Kumi.</i>

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:32.930
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:37.800
<i>– Kumi!</i>
<i>– Oh!</i>

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:46.860
<i>What do you mean,</i>
<i>"don't worry," dummy?</i>

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:52.500
After that, I was suddenly
conscious of Machida

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:57.530
and I couldn't be around him
the same way anymore.

00:11:58.430 --> 00:11:59.130
Kumi...

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:02.430
Yup, yup, I understand.

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:08.060
Hey Mitsuki, what should I do first?
Teach me! Please!

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:10.330
What? Th-That's...

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:11.260
Mitsuki!

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:20.630
Oh yeah! Let's first
do research on Machida!

00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:23.160
How are we
going to do research?

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:25.560
Don't worry, leave it to me!

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:41.460
<i>And thus, it will now become</i>
<i>the most suitable season</i>

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:44.400
<i>for studying and sports.</i>

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:47.400
<i>Everybody, please engage in</i>
<i>your interests with your best efforts.</i>

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:48.930
Hey, you!

00:12:49.060 --> 00:12:50.230
W-What?!

00:12:51.630 --> 00:12:52.800
W-What is it?

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:56.230
I'm doing a program called
"The Rumored Handsome Boy in Town."

00:12:56.260 --> 00:12:57.830
Can I interview you?

00:12:57.960 --> 00:12:59.560
R-Right now?

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:04.360
Here we go. Let's do this
interview at once.

00:13:04.560 --> 00:13:06.700
To be frank...
Do you have a girlfriend?

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:08.160
I don't have one.

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:10.260
What is your preferred type?

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:11.660
Nothing in particular.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:13.230
What is your favorite food?

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:14.560
Umm...

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:17.260
It's hamburger. Can I go now?

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:19.330
My homeroom is about to begin.

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:22.630
Yeah, thanks.
See you later, Machida.

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:26.000
No problem... Wait!
How did you know my name?

00:13:27.460 --> 00:13:29.100
Sh-She's gone?

00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:32.930
Machida doesn't seem to
have a girlfriend.

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:35.400
He doesn't have
a particular type of girl he likes,

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:37.300
and his favorite food is hamburger.

00:13:38.230 --> 00:13:39.930
You really are the master of romance.

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:41.600
How did you do the research?

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:43.260
Oh, that's a secret.

00:13:43.330 --> 00:13:44.900
And what's next?

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:45.860
Next?

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:47.530
What should I do?

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:49.030
A present.

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:53.560
Make a hamburger-shaped cookie
with a love letter as a present.

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:59.060
How about making a hamburger-shaped
cookie with a love letter as a present?

00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:03.000
Love letter?
I've never written one.

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:04.900
Leave it to me!

00:14:05.060 --> 00:14:06.800
I'm not involved in this, okay?

00:14:12.130 --> 00:14:13.900
Here comes Machida.

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:15.400
Y-Yeah.

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:18.530
Umm... Next is Literature class.

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:21.760
He noticed!

00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:23.030
Y-Yeah.

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:27.430
He noticed the love letter!

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:28.360
Yeah...

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:30.300
He's reading it, he's reading it!

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:43.730
What? What happened?

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:45.060
I don't know.

00:14:45.330 --> 00:14:47.760
Maybe he thinks that
it's somebody's practical joke.

00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:48.530
What?!

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:56.400
What's wrong, Kumi?

00:14:56.460 --> 00:14:58.060
But I'm embarrassed!

00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:00.860
Don't say a thing like that.
Come on!

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:19.330
I wonder if Machida will come.

00:15:19.760 --> 00:15:22.360
It's fine, I'm sure it'll go well.

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:24.200
Okay then, I'll leave now.

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:24.930
What?!

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:28.030
Wait, aren't you going
to stay with me?

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:30.160
Isn't it a problem if I stay with you?

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:31.730
It's not a problem.

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:34.230
Well, maybe it is a problem.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:37.830
But I'm just uneasy being alone!

00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:38.700
Please!

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:40.200
O-Okay.

00:15:45.930 --> 00:15:49.000
<i>Mr. Machida, although</i>
<i>from the shadows,</i>

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:50.830
<i>there's something I would like</i>
<i>to say to you.</i>

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:55.700
<i>Therefore, please come to</i>
<i>the back of the gymnasium today.</i>

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:59.060
<i>From a young girl who thinks of you.</i>

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:05.830
It's possible. This weird sentence
would be possible for Koyama.

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:08.260
But if I'm wrong...

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:12.200
<i>Caught you, caught you!</i>

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:17.300
I'm going to be a laughing stock.

00:16:28.930 --> 00:16:30.060
I'm going home!

00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:31.200
Hey, hey!

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:34.230
Why? Let's wait a little bit longer.

00:16:34.530 --> 00:16:35.330
But...

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:37.600
Little bit longer! Okay, Kumi?

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:40.000
Yeah...

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:45.200
Please Takuto!
Bring Machida over.

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:53.060
I know, even I...
But Kumi is serious!

00:16:53.300 --> 00:16:54.860
I can't pretend to ignore her!

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:58.630
I was to support Kumi
so her love would come true!

00:16:59.960 --> 00:17:01.430
All right, all right.

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:05.060
I won't say this and that anymore,
do your best in your own way.

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:07.730
Thank you!
Then, you'll bring Machida over?

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:10.200
Meroko already went to bring him here.

00:17:13.730 --> 00:17:16.360
Wait! Please wait!

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:17.800
Dang it.

00:17:17.830 --> 00:17:20.530
Why does it fly away when
there's not even a wind?!

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:23.100
That's because I caught it.

00:17:25.460 --> 00:17:27.360
Wait!

00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:35.730
Oh?

00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:45.130
M-Machida!

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:48.060
Y-You were waiting for me until now.

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:50.560
You think that much of me?

00:17:51.660 --> 00:17:54.560
Show your courage...now!

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:03.800
U-U-Umm...Machida...actually...you know...

00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:12.000
Sorry, Koyama.
I...didn't realize...

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:13.160
Huh?

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:14.400
I get it.

00:18:14.430 --> 00:18:15.960
You didn't have the
courage to say it alone,

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:17.130
so you had Saginomiya...

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:18.700
What?! U-Umm...

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:21.330
But it's wrong to have a girl say it.

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:23.230
As a man, I have to say it himself!

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:24.560
Koyama!

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:25.660
Y-Yes.

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:27.230
If you don't mind,
please go out with me!

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:28.830
First as friends.

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:32.700
W-What is happening?

00:18:32.730 --> 00:18:34.630
I told you something like
this was gonna happen!

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:37.560
U-Umm... That's not it, Machida!
It's...

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:46.960
K-Kumi! Wait!

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:49.730
Kumi!

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:52.600
W-What in the world is happening?

00:18:52.660 --> 00:18:53.900
Don't you understand?

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:56.760
You made a mistake in
the person you confessed to! Jeez!

00:19:17.560 --> 00:19:18.360
Kumi...

00:19:26.460 --> 00:19:28.800
Machida misunderstood.

00:19:29.430 --> 00:19:31.600
Let's go back and clearly
explain to him, okay?

00:19:34.030 --> 00:19:38.200
I can't. I'm not even
on Machida's mind.

00:19:38.430 --> 00:19:40.100
That's not true.

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:41.960
It's true! It's so true!

00:19:42.330 --> 00:19:45.330
It's because I'm not feminine at all!

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:49.200
I'm rough and my hobby
is judo of all things.

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:53.530
The type of girl that Machida likes
is probably somebody like you!

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:57.260
Sorry. I'm not actually mad at you.

00:19:57.330 --> 00:20:01.760
Oh no, it's fine.
But you'll definitely regret it.

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:04.530
Because it happened to me.

00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:09.630
When Eichi left for America
I couldn't say it.

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:11.930
"I like you."

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:18.330
I'm really regretting
why I couldn't say that one thing.

00:20:20.530 --> 00:20:22.860
You didn't tell him
that you like him?

00:20:22.960 --> 00:20:25.200
Didn't I tell you last time?

00:20:25.460 --> 00:20:28.600
Oh? Sorry, I wasn't listening carefully.

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:31.300
But, do you now understand?

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:34.900
I'm...not an expert on romance.

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:39.900
You're right.
You don't want to regret it.

00:20:40.330 --> 00:20:43.700
Instead of thinking later that
I should have done this at that time...

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:46.960
Maybe it's better to have my say.

00:20:48.160 --> 00:20:51.430
Let's go back.
Let's go back and say it clearly.

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:52.600
That you like him.

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:59.660
Okay, it's another fax-mail from
radio name, "Girl Sanshiro,"

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:01.930
who sent us one earlier.

00:21:02.430 --> 00:21:04.160
"Hello Miss Full Moon."

00:21:04.460 --> 00:21:08.230
"I finally confessed to the boy
that I told you about last time."

00:21:08.300 --> 00:21:10.060
That's great.

00:21:10.360 --> 00:21:12.330
"There were all kinds of
misunderstandings,"

00:21:12.360 --> 00:21:16.300
"but we will be going out,
first as friends."

00:21:16.530 --> 00:21:17.960
"Please give me your support."

00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:19.100
Of course!

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:22.000
"P.S. I would like to make
a request to my friend"

00:21:22.030 --> 00:21:24.800
"who was not able to say 'I like you'"

00:21:24.830 --> 00:21:27.200
"to somebody she liked in the past,
but is working hard today."

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:29.200
Okay, here's the request from

00:21:29.230 --> 00:21:32.230
Miss Girl Sanshiro.

00:21:32.400 --> 00:21:35.400
Here's my "Eternal Snow."

00:23:07.330 --> 00:23:09.730
I-Izumi is...

00:23:10.060 --> 00:23:14.800
Izumi? Impossible, not that Izumi!
He's appeared in the human world?!

00:23:14.830 --> 00:23:16.060
That's the one!

00:23:16.100 --> 00:23:17.960
Ordered here by the
Division Chief of Death Spirits!

00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:21.860
He's checking up on us to see
if we're doing our job right!

00:23:22.060 --> 00:23:26.900
Damn! At such a bad time too!
It's Mitsuki's concert for her new song!

00:23:27.300 --> 00:23:32.060
Next time on Full Moon:
"The New Death Spirits,
Izumi and Jonathan"

00:23:32.530 --> 00:23:34.000
– Look forward to it!
– Look forward to it!
